From: stepfunc-droid <stepfunc-droid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 23:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: avoid hardware bitmaps for navigation keys

MT8173's PowerVR userspace stack has incomplete hardware-bitmap support.
The three-button navigation bar renders its key icons through
ShadowKeyDrawable, which builds an ARGB_8888 cache and then converts it
to Bitmap.Config.HARDWARE. On suez that conversion can produce visibly
corrupted navigation icons while the rest of the navigation bar remains
intact, and the corruption is also present in screenshots.

Keep the cached bitmap in ARGB_8888 instead. ShadowKeyDrawable still
caches the rendered icon, so this does not force per-frame regeneration;
HWUI can upload the software-backed bitmap through the normal texture
path when drawing it.
---
 .../systemui/statusbar/phone/ShadowKeyDrawable.java       | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/ShadowKeyDrawable.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/ShadowKeyDrawable.java
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/ShadowKeyDrawable.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/ShadowKeyDrawable.java
@@ -150,7 +150,6 @@ public class ShadowKeyDrawable extends Drawable {
             d.draw(canvas);
         }
 
-        bitmap = bitmap.copy(Bitmap.Config.HARDWARE, false);
         mState.mLastDrawnBitmap = bitmap;
         canvas.restore();
     }
